From: SF2000 Linux <sf2000@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mquickjs: declare js_date_constructor in mquickjs_priv.h

js_date_constructor is defined in mqjs.c and referenced from the generated
stdlib class tables, but has no header declaration.  The js2300 runtime
includes those tables directly, so the definition-before-use ordering inside
mqjs.c does not help.  Declare it next to the other date helpers.

--- a/mquickjs_priv.h
+++ b/mquickjs_priv.h
@@ -238,6 +238,9 @@ JSValue js_typed_array_set(JSContext *ctx, JSValue *this_val,
                            int argc, JSValue *argv);
 
+JSValue js_date_constructor(JSContext *ctx, JSValue *this_val,
+                            int argc, JSValue *argv);
+
 JSValue js_date_valueOf(JSContext *ctx, JSValue *this_val,
                         int argc, JSValue *argv);
 
